# Both bundles in this directory are downloaded at run time, version-matched to
# what the run is actually testing, and must never be committed:
#   kv_store.mpk  — from the pinned core release's kv-store-test-fixture.mpk
#                   (.github/workflows/merobox-sync.yml)
#   curb-app.mpk  — from the app registry
#                   (.github/workflows/merobox-chat-sync.yml)
# A committed copy is a copy that goes stale silently: the vendored kv_store.wasm
# drifted 10 release candidates behind the node, and a wasm that predates the
# node's host ABI leaves the joining node on the all-ones "uninitialized" hash
# forever — which reads as a cross-node sync bug.
#
# ⚠️ `.mpk`, not `.wasm`. core 0.11.0-rc.31 (core#3652) made a raw module a 500
# on dev install — `not a signed application bundle: <path>` — because an
# application id is derived from a bundle's package and signer, so a bare module
# has no identity to install under. Both patterns stay ignored so a leftover
# `.wasm` from before that cannot be committed either.
*.mpk
*.wasm
